# The pc platform's bonus round test (#1093, docs/platforms.md): boot.keys's
# Start and A through the logos, the menus and New Game into Jungle Jam (the
# first level, frame 520), then its first room played to the bonus platform:
# a lizard kills Crash (~1040), a pit by the first checkpoint (~1985); on the
# "?" platform at frame ~2440, into the bonus round (~2560). In it, crates
# broken, and the life crate (above the iron arrow crate) broken from it at
# frame 3676, which crashed the host until ClampFrame's NULL_READs
# (pickups.hpp: the new extra life's bank read while NULL). Out by the exit
# pad (~4200) onto the bonus platform, then on, dying twice (~4720, ~4935).
# tools/boottest.py `screens` played it on mGBA for tests/bonus_mgba_screens.json.
# Written by playing it under gdb (the keys from Crash's position).
# A line `FRAME KEYS` holds KEYS from FRAME on (platform/pc/src/input.c).
